---
/**
 * One hundred requests through a cascade, drawn so that all three of the unit's
 * claims about routing are visible at once.
 *
 * Every request passes through the small model first — that is the shape people
 * get wrong, and it is why the arithmetic panel charges the small model on all
 * hundred rather than on the eighty-eight that stopped there. The figures in
 * the panel are the ones the prose quotes and they are one multiplication each:
 * 100 × 1.00 = 100.00 against 100 × 0.02 = 2.00 plus 12 × 1.00 = 12.00, giving
 * 14.00, which is a little over a seventh. Change any of them and the prose is
 * wrong.
 *
 * The two costs that routing adds rather than removes are drawn as prominently
 * as the saving: the escalated twelve now wait 2.2 s instead of 2.0, and the
 * dashed panel holds the requests the gate misjudged, which come back confident
 * and unflagged.
 *
 * Nothing is carried by colour: each branch is labelled with its count, each
 * box states its own timing and price in words, and the failure path is dashed
 * and says what it is. Decorative on its own, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure`
 * supplies the accessible name and the description.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 368" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
  <text
    x="12"
    y="18"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="14"
    font-weight="700">One hundred requests, small model first</text
  >
  <text x="12" y="32" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="9"
    >prices in whatever unit you like — the large model costs fifty times the
    small one</text
  >

  <!-- Everything arrives. -->
  <rect
    x="12"
    y="118"
    width="86"
    height="44"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-paper stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"></rect>
  <text
    x="55"
    y="140"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="15"
    font-weight="700">100</text
  >
  <text
    x="55"
    y="154"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="8">requests in</text
  >

  <g class="stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.5">
    <line x1="98" y1="140" x2="122" y2="140"></line>
    <path d="M118 136 L124 140 L118 144" class="fill-none"></path>
  </g>

  <!-- Every single one of them goes through the small model. -->
  <rect
    x="126"
    y="110"
    width="118"
    height="60"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-accent-2-soft stroke-accent-2"
    stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
  <text
    x="185"
    y="130"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="11"
    font-weight="700">small model</text
  >
  <text
    x="185"
    y="144"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="8">on hardware you own</text
  >
  <text
    x="185"
    y="157"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="8">0.2 s, 0.02 each</text
  >

  <g class="stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.5">
    <line x1="244" y1="140" x2="258" y2="140"></line>
    <path d="M254 136 L260 140 L254 144" class="fill-none"></path>
  </g>

  <!-- The gate reads what came back. -->
  <rect
    x="262"
    y="112"
    width="84"
    height="56"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-paper-sunken stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"></rect>
  <text
    x="304"
    y="132"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="11"
    font-weight="700">gate</text
  >
  <text
    x="304"
    y="146"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="8">was this one</text
  >
  <text
    x="304"
    y="157"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="8">beyond it?</text
  >

  <!-- Escalated. -->
  <g class="fill-none stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.5">
    <polyline points="346,126 372,126 372,72 394,72"></polyline>
    <path d="M390 68 L396 72 L390 76"></path>
  </g>
  <text
    x="366"
    y="100"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink font-mono"
    font-size="9">12 sent on</text
  >

  <rect
    x="400"
    y="44"
    width="224"
    height="58"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-accent-soft stroke-accent"
    stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
  <text
    x="412"
    y="64"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="11"
    font-weight="700">12 escalated to the large model</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="78" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >hosted elsewhere, 2.0 s and 1.00 each</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="92" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >so these twelve now wait 2.2 s, not 2.0</text
  >

  <!-- Answered where they landed. -->
  <g class="fill-none stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.5">
    <polyline points="346,154 372,154 372,209 394,209"></polyline>
    <path d="M390 205 L396 209 L390 213"></path>
  </g>
  <text
    x="366"
    y="192"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink font-mono"
    font-size="9">88 stay here</text
  >

  <rect
    x="400"
    y="180"
    width="224"
    height="58"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-accent-2-soft stroke-accent-2"
    stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
  <text
    x="412"
    y="200"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="11"
    font-weight="700">88 answered by the small model</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="214" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >0.2 s each, nothing leaves the building</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="228" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >this branch is where the saving comes from</text
  >

  <!-- The ones the gate misjudged, drawn as a failure: dashed, and unflagged. -->
  <g
    class="fill-none stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.5"
    stroke-dasharray="4 3"
  >
    <line x1="490" y1="238" x2="490" y2="248"></line>
    <path d="M486 244 L490 250 L494 244" stroke-dasharray="0"></path>
  </g>

  <rect
    x="400"
    y="252"
    width="224"
    height="64"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-paper-sunken stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"
    stroke-dasharray="4 3"></rect>
  <text
    x="412"
    y="272"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="10"
    font-weight="700">and the gate is not perfect</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="286" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >some of the eighty-eight were beyond it.</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="297" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >They came back confident anyway, and</text
  >
  <text x="412" y="308" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="8"
    >nothing in the system says otherwise.</text
  >

  <!-- What the hundred cost, either way. Kept clear of the lower branch, which
       turns at x=372. -->
  <rect
    x="12"
    y="206"
    width="352"
    height="118"
    rx="6"
    class="fill-paper stroke-rule"
    stroke-width="1"></rect>
  <text
    x="24"
    y="226"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="11"
    font-weight="700">what the hundred cost</text
  >

  <g class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="9">
    <text x="24" y="246">all hundred to the large model</text>
    <text x="24" y="266">cascade — the small model, all hundred</text>
    <text x="24" y="280">cascade — the large model, the twelve</text>
  </g>
  <g class="fill-ink font-mono" font-size="9" text-anchor="end">
    <text x="352" y="246">100 × 1.00 = 100.00</text>
    <text x="352" y="266">100 × 0.02 = 2.00</text>
    <text x="352" y="280">12 × 1.00 = 12.00</text>
  </g>

  <line x1="24" y1="288" x2="352" y2="288" class="stroke-rule" stroke-width="1"
  ></line>

  <text
    x="24"
    y="302"
    class="fill-ink font-mono"
    font-size="9"
    font-weight="700">cascade, total</text
  >
  <text
    x="352"
    y="302"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink font-mono"
    font-size="9"
    font-weight="700">14.00</text
  >
  <text x="24" y="316" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="8"
    >the small model is paid on all hundred, not only the eighty-eight</text
  >

  <text
    x="12"
    y="344"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="12"
    font-weight="700"
    >Just over seven times cheaper — and the twelve hardest requests got slower.</text
  >
  <text x="12" y="358" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="9"
    >Both of those are the arrangement working exactly as designed.</text
  >
</svg>
